    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0254" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.115 St 21/343: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-19T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1924—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>187. L–85, for Logan. Your L–151 of April 28. Standard Oil Company suggests a
                    compromise based in principle upon equal division <pb facs="0255" n="161"
                        xml:id="pg161"/> of proceeds from sale at auction of five tank steamers and
                    of balance remaining in operator’s fund after reimbursement of all of Company’s
                    expenditures made under the Tanker Agreement. Montagu Piesse<anchor n="84"
                        xml:id="d117-f1"/> has been instructed to discuss the question with you and
                    Leon Fraser.<anchor n="85" xml:id="d117-f2"/> Copies of Standard Oil Company’s
                    letters to Department and to Piesse were mailed to you on June 17.<anchor n="86"
                        xml:id="d117-f3"/> The proposal is silent in regard to disposition of sum
                    paid by German Government to D. A. P. G.; but aside from this point, on which
                    further inquiry is being made of Standard Oil, the proposal is evidently within
                    scope of the agreement as amended and decisions of the Separation
                    Commission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d117-f1" n="84" xml:id="d117-f1-content">
                <p>Legal representative in London of the Standard Oil Co.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d117-f2" n="85" xml:id="d117-f2-content">
                <p>General counsel for the Dawes Plan and representative in Paris of the Agent
                    General, reparation payments.</p>
            </note>
